## Clean Code skills

The 14 `py-*`, `ts-*`, `python-clean-code`, and `typescript-clean-code` skills are derived from
[ertugrul-dmr/clean-code-skills](https://github.com/ertugrul-dmr/clean-code-skills), used under the MIT License.

Changes made:

- Skill names given `py-` / `ts-` prefixes, because Claude Code requires unique skill names and the
  upstream Python and TypeScript sets both define `boy-scout`, `clean-comments`, `clean-functions`,
  `clean-general`, `clean-names`, and `clean-tests`.
- The non-standard `when_to_use` frontmatter field folded into `description`, which is the field
  Claude Code actually reads when deciding whether to load a skill.
- Cross-references between skills updated to the prefixed names.
- Two sections added, because the upstream set does not cover them: the stepdown rule
  ("code reads top-down") in `py-clean-functions` and `ts-clean-functions`, and composition over
  inheritance in `py-clean-general` and `ts-clean-general`. Both are reflected in the aggregate
  skills' rule lists and quick-reference tables.
- Repackaged as a Claude Code plugin.

Skill bodies are otherwise unmodified. The upstream MIT license text follows.

